Field Type Required Meaning <code>type</code> enum yes <code>error</code>, <code>warning</code>, <code>info</code> or <code>disclosure</code> <code>code</code> string yes A code from the registry <code>origin</code> enum conditional Who wrote <code>content</code>: <code>gateway</code> (the default when <code>args</code> is absent) or <code>counterparty</code>. REQUIRED whenever <code>args</code> is present. <code>content</code> LangText yes Multilingual text keyed by BCP 47 tag, for example <code>{"hi-IN": "…", "en-IN": "…"}</code>. A gateway-written <code>content</code> never contains counterparty text. <code>args</code> array no Values inserted at <code>{name}</code> placeholders in <code>content</code>, each <code>{name, origin, text}</code>. A counterparty value (an item name, a fee label) travels only here, with <code>origin: counterparty</code>. <code>param</code> string no RFC 9535 JSONPath into the returned resource <code>resolution</code> enum yes What the agent may do next (see Resolution) <pre><code>{
  "type": "warning",
  "code": "payment_in_doubt",
  "content": {
    "en-IN": "Debit status unknown. Reconciling with the PSP. Do not retry with a new key."
  },
  "param": "$.payment.status",
  "resolution": "recoverable"
}
</code></pre> <p>The first message of every checkout session is the <code>ai_disclosure</code> message (<code>type: disclosure</code>), which carries the agent's AI notice in the principal's language and points (<code>param: $.ai_disclosure</code>) at the session's typed routes to a human.</p> <p>For a message with <code>type: disclosure</code> and a code registered below with that type (<code>sponsored_listing</code>, <code>sponsorship_undeclared</code> and <code>prior_price_claim</code>), an agent that presents the session to a principal MUST present the fixed phrase for that code from Disclosure phrases, in the principal's language, next to what <code>param</code> names, with the item's name, as labelled seller text, taken from the session line whose item is the <code>catalogue[]</code> entry's <code>item_id</code>, never from <code>args</code>. It fills the phrase's slots from the <code>Disclosures.catalogue[]</code> entry that <code>param</code> names. It MUST NOT summarise, hide or drop the message, and it hands off to a human rather than present it in a reduced form. It never reads the message's <code>content</code> in place of the fixed phrase. A <code>type: disclosure</code> message with an unregistered code is treated as <code>info</code>: the agent records it and does not read it verbatim. <code>ai_disclosure</code> keeps its own rule.</p>

Field Rule <code>firm</code> <code>true</code>: the offeror is bound if the offer is accepted before <code>expires_at</code>. <code>false</code>: an indicative quote, which is an invitation to treat. <code>subject_to_principal_approval</code> MUST be <code>true</code> when the emitting agent's guard returned <code>needs_escalation</code>. The schema then forces <code>firm: false</code>. <code>term_sheet</code>, <code>all_in_total</code> <code>all_in_total</code> MUST equal <code>term_sheet.all_in_total</code>. <code>valid_from</code>, <code>expires_at</code> <code>expires_at</code> is absolute, never a relative TTL. <code>expires_at − valid_from</code> MUST be at least the effective <code>min_offer_validity</code> (floor <code>PT5M</code>). Otherwise <code>NEG_FALSE_URGENCY</code>. <code>inventory_hold_until</code> How long stock is held for this offer <code>acceptance_manner</code> The constant <code>bacp.neg.accept</code>. Every other form of acceptance is non-conforming. <code>acceptance_revocation</code> REQUIRED when <code>firm</code> is <code>true</code>, with no default: <code>allowed_until_receipt</code> or <code>waived</code>. A gateway MUST NOT insert or normalise the value before hashing. In this version every receiver refuses <code>allowed_until_receipt</code> with <code>capabilities_incompatible</code>. See Acceptance revocation. <code>waiver_basis</code> REQUIRED when <code>acceptance_revocation</code> is <code>waived</code>: a <code>DocumentRef</code> with <code>doc_type</code> <code>contract</code> or <code>rfq</code> and a <code>hash</code>. <code>extends</code> The hash of an earlier offer by the same offeror that this offer re-issues with a later <code>expires_at</code>. Terms MUST be identical. <code>agreed_issues[]</code> JSON Pointers already in <code>Agree</code>. They narrow the open set and do not bind. <code>rfq_parent_id</code>, <code>bid_deposit_ref</code>, <code>auction_id</code> RFQ and auction links <code>sender_log_seq</code>, <code>sender_log_prev</code>, <code>protocol_terms</code> REQUIRED when <code>firm</code> is <code>true</code> and on every bid: the offer's position in the sender's own chain, the previous entry's hash, and the protocol terms that govern it. <code>expires_at</code> is a receipt deadline at the offeror (see Expiry). offer.b2c-counter.json (seller's firm counter-offer, round 2; valid shape; receivers refuse allowed_until_receipt in this version)<pre><code>{
